# Easy Roasted Broccoli

Simple high-heat roasted broccoli with crisp, deeply browned edges and a tender interior.

## info
* About 25 minutes
* 4 servings

## ingredients
* 1 head broccoli, cut into 1½- to 2-inch florets (about 1 pound / 450 g florets)
* 3 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil
* Kosher salt, to taste
* Freshly ground black pepper, to taste

## steps
1. Line a rimmed baking sheet with aluminum foil. Place an oven rack in the upper position and preheat the oven to 500°F (260°C). Put the baking sheet in the oven while it preheats.
2. In a large bowl, toss the broccoli florets with the olive oil. Season with kosher salt and black pepper.
3. Carefully transfer the broccoli to the hot baking sheet and spread into a single layer.
4. Roast for about 20 minutes, or until the broccoli is tender and deeply browned in spots.
5. For browning mostly on one side, leave the broccoli undisturbed while roasting. For more even browning, toss or flip the broccoli halfway through cooking.
6. Serve immediately.

## notes
* Preheating the baking sheet helps develop better browning.
* High heat creates crisp edges and caramelized flavor.
* Adjust salt and pepper to taste before serving.

